  {
    "category": "ai agents",
    "prompt": "### Image Prompt (No Title or Description in Image)\n\nCreate a clean, beginner-friendly **vector-style infographic** that visually explains how OpenAI Agents dynamically adjust behavior in real-time. **Do not include any title, heading, or descriptive text** within the image. Focus entirely on graphical metaphors and modular structure.\n\n---\n\n### Visual Purpose\nHelp beginners intuitively grasp how OpenAI agents operate in healthcare, productivity, or technical systems. The visual must depict the **agent logic** through a clean, metaphor-rich, and scannable diagram—free of any top-labeling text.\n\n---\n\n### Design Guidelines\n\n1. **Layout & Composition**\n   - Use a balanced, infographic-style layout with a central **AI logic core** (e.g., microchip or modular processor).\n   - Surround or connect this with visual panels and arrows showing behavior adjustment.\n\n2. **Core Visual Structure**\n   - **Central Agent Node**: Abstract representation of the AI agent (e.g., chip, logic block).\n   - **Instruction Panels** (around or vertically stacked near the node):\n     - **Purpose**: Use teal green labeled visuals like icons or pills with \"Assist,\" \"Interpret,\" \"Decide.\"\n     - **Tone**: Icons in deep navy (e.g., smiley, neutral, avatar).\n     - **Decision Strategy**: Charcoal logic blocks with arrows, leading to ✅ or ⚠️ output icons.\n\n3. **Data Flow Representation**\n   - **Left side**: Inputs like user messages, clinical notes (speech bubbles, document icons).\n   - **Center**: Logic flow inside the agent (arrows, processors, conditional nodes).\n   - **Right side**: Outputs such as AI replies, alerts, and visual analytics (chat bubbles, warning signs, bar graphs).\n\n4. **Color & Style**\n   - Background: Flat **sky blue** for calm tone  \n   - Visual elements: Rounded, soft edges; minimal shadows  \n   - Style: Flat vector, professional, modern"
